a timestamp string. After PATCH of a document there is an entry with action 'document.updated'. After DELETE there is 'document.deleted'.\n\nStructure:\n- Top-level: let app: ReturnType<typeof createApp>; and beforeEach(() => { app = createApp(); });\n- Helper async function registerAndLogin(username: string): Promise<string> that registers {username, password: 'pw-' + username} then logs in and returns the token. Note register of duplicate in same test not needed; app is fresh per test.\n- Helper async function makeFolder(token: string, name: string): Promise<string> that POSTs /folders and returns body.id.\n- Use await request(app).post('/auth/register').send({...}) style. Assert status with expect(res.status).toBe(...).\n\nWrite these describe blocks with these tests:\ndescribe('auth'): register returns 201 with id and username; register without password returns 400; duplicate username returns 409; login returns 200 with token; login with wrong password returns 401; request to POST /folders without token returns 401; request with garbage token 'Bearer nope' returns 401.\ndescribe('folders'): create folder 201 with parentId null; create with missing name 400; create nested folder with parentId set returns 201 and parentId equals parent id; GET folder returns 200 with name and folders/documents arrays; GET unknown folder id 'nope' returns 404; PATCH rename returns 200 and new name; DELETE returns 204 and subsequent GET returns 404; create folder with nonexistent parentId returns 404.\ndescribe('documents'): create via POST /folders/:id/documents returns 201 with title/content/folderId; create via POST /documents with folderId in body returns 201; create with missing title returns 400; create with nonexistent folder returns 404; GET document returns 200 with content; GET unknown document returns 404; PATCH updates title and content returns 200; DELETE returns 204 then GET 404.\ndescribe('activity'): creating then updating then deleting a document produces log entries 'document.created', 'document.updated', 'document.deleted' each with resourceType 'document' and correct resourceId; GET /activity without token returns 401.\n\nEvery test creates its own users/folders via the helpers. Return only the complete file content.\" > /tmp/light_crud_tests.ts 2>/tmp/light_err.log; echo \"EXIT:$?\"; wc -l /tmp/light_crud_tests.ts","description":"Delegate CRUD test suite to light worker","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":620,"cache_read_input_tokens":33824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":620},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7263746d-7ad6-42f4-9cde-e93144828090","uuid":"497cb16d-9e07-45d5-b002-cc929a961d60","request_id":"req_011CdP4L5VWreHcJy7op8jVp"}
